the justice department is launching an  investigation of the phoenix police  department  over allegations of using excessive  force now this is a biden  administration's third investigation of  a law enforcement agency  following probes of the minneapolis and  louisville police  police departments attorney general  merrick garland says the review in  phoenix  will examine any pattern of unlawful  policing including  deadly force discriminatory behavior and  retaliation  jeff begues looks at the history that  led to this new investigation  in recent years phoenix police have  gotten a reputation for too  often using excessive force  one case in particular stands out in  2019  officers pointed guns at a black family  threatening to shoot the father in front  of his fiance and children  after one of the toddlers took a doll  from a dollar store  that case and others in the arizona city  will now be part of the justice  department's pattern or practice  investigation  federal civil rights investigators will  assess all types of use of force by  phoenix police  including deadly force the investigation  will determine whether the phoenix  police department engages in a pattern  or practice of violations of the  constitution  or federal law the training itself the  content  was the absolute worst training i've  ever had in 2019  cbs this morning investigated police  practices in the city  according to a report by the arizona  republic the year before  phoenix police had 44 officer involved  shootings  the most in the country and most of  those incidents involve black  or native americans there are some  people who  think well are phoenix police trigger  happy  there are some people who think a lot of  things my agency is unafraid of the  truth  if there's something we can learn let's  learn it let's fix it the department  enacted changes in tactics  including ending neck restraints and  tracking when officers draw their  weapons why does the place of ice exist  even mandated implicit bias training  which didn't  seem to leave an impression on some  officers who spoke freely after we  agreed to conceal their identity  will it change how you do your job no  why not  i don't think i was doing it incorrectly  to begin with on thursday  chief williams acknowledged that there  was room for improvement so i'm looking  forward to them  seeing what we've done right and also  what we can improve on  the doj investigation will likely take  more than  a year to complete you can expect more  of these types of  pattern or practice investigations from  this attorney general the previous  administration all but  abandoned federal oversight of local  police departments  glad all right jeff looking forward to  the results of that investigation thank  you very much
 

